archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4003514Z ^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4004556Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4005315Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4005574Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4006115Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4007087Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4007410Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4007642Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4008207Z    if you are ready to continue.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4008471Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4009069Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4010119Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4011019Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4011768Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4012093Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4012421Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4012924Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4013337Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4014096Z    can use Nix.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4014377Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4014585Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4014909Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4015451Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4016544Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4019573Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4019779Z I will:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4020036Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4020567Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4021407Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4022421Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4023026Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4023430Z  - install Nix in /nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4023815Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4024324Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4024804Z    /root
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4036854Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4037681Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4047951Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4048511Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4049348Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4050277Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4050965Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4068319Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4068992Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4079591Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4080454Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4080896Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4081281Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4081510Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4081798Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4082008Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4082458Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4082692Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4082811Z If you would like to
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4083093Z see the output, try like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4083455Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4083800Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4084448Z   $ sh ./install-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4084634Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4084668Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4084902Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4092152Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T19:59:29.4092834Z been installed on this system.
